  "raw": {
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34333": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Geosciences with additional title of STEM Center Director",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Lecturer in Geosciences with additional title of STEM Center Director Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Lecturer in Geosciences with additional title of STEM Center Director Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates should review and complete the online application that requires uploading curriculum vitae; letter of application; statement of teaching philosophy; and list of three references with contact information to include mailing address, e-mail address, and telephone numbers at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34322 Posting Details Position Details Title Lecturer in Geosciences with additional title of STEM Center Director Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Northwest Geosciences Location Northwest Position Summary Review date begins October 21, 2026: (Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee). Final date: November 4, 2026: Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. The Department of Biology and Geosciences within the College of Arts, Sciences, and Education at Indiana University Northwest seeks to fill a Lecturer in Geology and STEM Center Director position. The position is a full-time, 12-month appointment. The teaching load is to be half time during the Fall, Spring, and Summer (a 2/2/1 FTE equivalent) with the remainder devoted to directing STEM Center programs. Lecturer in Geology Teaching Responsibilities: We seek a broadly educated geologist with demonstrated commitment to teaching at the undergraduate level. This position will contribute to majors in geoscience, environmental science, and sustainability, as well as general education courses. The individual will have a focus on STEM student success, the ability to implement sound pedagogy for both in-person and online instruction, and a commitment to undergraduate engagement. Teaching responsibilities will include introductory and early-career courses in earth science, geology, or geography (including geographic information systems [ GIS ]) and upper-level geology and geography courses based on the successful candidate’s areas of expertise and departmental needs. Course assignments may include courses in GIS , field methods and laboratory techniques, and climate change science, and foundational courses at the 100- and 200-level including introductory courses in Earth science, historical geology, and a first-year seminar in geoscience. Expertise in GIS , surficial processes and systems (geomorphology, Quaternary, glacial/climate systems, soils), and other expertise that will complement departmental expertise in mineralogy, ocean science, petrology, sedimentology/stratigraphy, and structural geology is particularly valued. With the Fall 2026 reorganization, the Departments of Geosciences and Biology merged and offer B.S. and B.A. degrees in Biological and Physical Sciences that will include majors in biology, environmental science (B.S. only), and geoscience, and an online B.A. degree in sustainability, shared among five IU regional campuses. Additionally, the department contributes to programs in science education and a master’s program in liberal studies. Core teaching responsibilities include a 6-hour equivalent per semester teaching load in the fall and spring semesters, and a 3-hour equivalent teaching load in the summer in face-to-face or online modalities. The teaching load may be unequally distributed based on departmental needs. Additionally, the successful candidate will actively engage in service to the department, campus, discipline, and the community. STEM Center Responsibilities : The STEM Center Director will: Provide leadership in developing/maintaining an effective, integrated approach to support student success in STEM working closely with internal and community college stakeholders. Work closely with STEM faculty and key campus administrators to enhance outreach and recruitment efforts of students in STEM programs. Advocate for student retention and success initiatives across campus and assume a leadership role in developing a culture of belonging and success for all STEM students. Engage with high schools, community, and industry stakeholders to enhance student interest in STEM and increase student knowledge of, and access to, STEM employment opportunities during the school year, summer, and after graduation. Coordinate services and activities with STEM faculty and existing campus support services in counseling, advising, tutoring, mentoring, and career services to maximize resources and achieve project goals. Plan, develop, and integrate innovative support services and activities designed to facilitate the success of STEM students. Prepare regular reports on the center’s overall effectiveness for project and campus leadership in accordance with the approved evaluation plan. ABOUT INDIANA UNIVERSITY NORTHWEST One of ten campuses of Indiana University, IU Northwest is located in metropolitan Northwest Indiana, approximately 30 miles southeast of Chicago and 10 miles from the Indiana Dunes National Park. The campus has a student population of approximately 3,200 degree-seeking students and more than 30,000 alumni, most of whom remain in the Northwest Indiana region, and has been recognized by the Department of Education as a minority and Hispanic serving institution. The campus offers Associate, Baccalaureate, and Master’s degrees from the College of Arts, Sciences & Education, the College of Health and Human Services, and the College of Business & Public Affairs. The campus is also home to IU School of Medicine-Northwest-Gary, the region’s only four-year medical doctorate program. As a student-centered campus, IU Northwest is committed to academic excellence characterized by a love of ideas and achievement in learning, discovery, creativity, research and community engagement. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications: M.S. in Geology or closely related field by May 31, 2027. Demonstrated ability to teach introductory/early career courses in earth science, geology, or geography, and majors’ courses based on candidate expertise and departmental needs – including courses in GIS , field methods, and historical geology. Demonstrated ability to work collegially with students, fellow faculty, and staff. Demonstrated ability to drive multiple projects to successful completion. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated interest in involving undergraduate students in high impact activities that engage and prepare students for advancement. Ability to incorporate modern technologies in teaching, and/or mentored student projects. Willingness to assist the department and campus in its ability to reach strategic goals, as specified in IUN’s strategic plan. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in initiating new ideas and addressing student, faculty, or staff concerns. Excellent collaboration and team building skills. Five years of experience/leadership in STEM education or industry; experience or familiarity with programs or services to encourage success of low-income, and other STEM majors in skills/competencies. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to the search committee chair: Kristin Huysken, Ph.D., 3400 Broadway, Gary, IN 46408, khuysken@iu.edu Additional Qualifications All candidates must be eligible to work in the United States as of the position start date. The department is unable to sponsor visas for this position. For questions about work eligibility, the search committee can connect you with the IU Office of International Services. Salary and Rank Salary is commensurate with experience and education. Special Instructions Interested candidates should review and complete the online application that requires uploading curriculum vitae; letter of application; statement of teaching philosophy; and list of three references with contact information to include mailing address, e-mail address, and telephone numbers at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34322 For Best Consideration Date Expected Start Date 07/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101675-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy List Of References Optional Documents Other Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34178": {
      "title": "Dean of the College of Business and Public Affairs",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Dean of the College of Business and Public Affairs Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Dean of the College of Business and Public Affairs Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Title Dean of the College of Business and Public Affairs Appointment Status Tenure Department IU Northwest Office Of Academic Affairs Location Northwest Position Summary Indiana University Northwest, one of nine campuses of Indiana University, is seeking a dynamic, innovative, and fairness-focused leader as Dean of the newly formed College of Business and Public Affairs. The campus, located in metropolitan Northwest Indiana, is approximately 30 miles southeast of Chicago and 10 miles from the Indiana Dunes National Park. The Dean of the College of Business and Public Affairs reports to the Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs. The IU Northwest College of Business and Public Affairs houses the School of Business and Economics and the School of Public and Environmental Affairs and provides students a premier undergraduate and graduate education through its fully accredited programs in Business ( AACSB ) and Public Affairs ( NASPAA ). The Dean serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the college, providing visionary leadership and strategic direction. The Dean is responsible for overseeing academic programs, faculty affairs, budget management, and ensuring compliance with accreditation standards across disciplines. The Dean in collaboration with faculty and other university leaders plays a critical part in advancing the campus’s mission of academic excellence, innovation, student success, and community engagement. Appointment Status Tenure-line with an Administrative assignment, tenurable in any of departments within Indiana University Northwest’s College of Business and Public Affairs (School of Business and Economics and School of Public and Environmental Affairs). Position Summary The position is a twelve-month appointment that will include a tenured faculty appointment in one of the academic programs offered in the College. Management: Supervise and provide leadership for the faculty and exempt and non-exempt staff in the College of Business and Public Affairs. Utilize continuous improvement strategies to ensure operational excellence. Manage a budget of approximately $4 million, advocating for resources to support faculty, staff and programmatic needs. Accreditation: Support accreditation efforts of each unit by keeping abreast of changing standards as well as facilitating the development of relevant programs and curricula that meet standards. Leadership: In concert with faculty, develop a clear mission, vision, and strategy for the newly formed College, emphasizing the campus and university commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, research with undergraduate students, and programmatic assessment to ensure continuous quality improvement. Represent the College to external stakeholders including alumni, donors, community partners, and accrediting bodies. Faculty and Staff Development: Utilize strategies that strengthen faculty and staff development and performance. Build upon an environment of participation, fairness, and stability, among faculty, staff, and students. Student Success: Develop strategies in collaboration with other units across campus to support the recruitment, retention, persistence and graduation of students in each undergraduate and graduate program. Curriculum and Academics: Supervise curriculum development, program evaluations, and the implementation of academic policies; ensure curricula and program portfolio aligns with regional needs and strategic priorities of the institution. Continue to advance and elevate the quality of teaching by implementing best practices, fostering faculty mentoring and development, and promoting continuous quality improvement, emphasizing curricula that is current, relevant, and prepares students for success in their chosen field. Work with deans from other regional campuses to develop and sustain collaborative academic programs. Teamwork: Foster the development of positive and productive relationships within the college; work effectively with the other academic Deans, the Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs and other leaders across campus, leaders from all campuses of Indiana University; and partner with external constituencies to ensure the success of our students and academic programs. Fund raising: Seek alternative forms of financial support such as external grants and other funding opportunities in concert with the Office of Sponsored Research, Office of Development and the Chancellor Procedures for Candidates The confidential review of applicant materials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Upload application materials which include a curriculum vita and letter describing your interest in and qualifications for the position. This letter should be no longer than 4 pages and should address the above topics. Basic Qualifications Required Qualifications: Terminal degree in a discipline finding its home in Indiana University Northwest’s College of Business and Public Affairs with credentials meriting appointment at the rank of full professor. Progressively responsible academic administrative experience. Demonstrated collaborative leadership, committed to supporting multiple perspectives in curricula, in student services, and in personnel and leadership decisions across the college, school, and department. Strong evidence of managerial experience directly supervising faculty/staff, developing an effective team, and fostering a culture of collegiality with a management style built on respect, communication, collaboration, and fairness. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching and research. A reputation for integrity, transparency, accountability, and enthusiasm. Experience with accreditation in the disciplines found in the College of Business and Public Affairs. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated knowledge of the opportunities and challenges facing higher education today A leadership style that is adaptable, collaborative, and decisive, and that can influence the community (internal and external) to identify, address, and overcome challenges. Financial acumen and proven abilities in budgetary and financial management. Interpersonal skills that enable effective relationships with all stakeholders, including other University leaders, alumni, advisory boards, professional officials, and leaders in the industries represented in the College of Business and Public Affairs. Department Contact for Questions This search is being managed by IU’s Executive Recruiting team. For questions related to this search or to nominate a candidate for this role, please email exesrch@iu.edu. Emails to this inbox are treated as confidential. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring, https://policies.iu.edu/policies/ua-01-non-discrimination/index.html Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Salary is commensurate with experience and education. Special Instructions For Best Consideration Date Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101651-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
